  "reveal": {
    "brief_voiced": "The killer was Effie Strange. The touch faltered twice. Fides tripped about the second minute of the touch; the green hand's own trip — a new hand's stumble convicts nobody, and the tower thinks no worse of it. But Patientia hung late where the method wanted her elsewhere, and no custom excuses it; that rope was in Effie Strange's keeping, and the hands that should have held it were free about the second minute of the touch. Dr Tobias Quill did not survive the office.\n\nAs to the why of it: Of Effie Strange, the playbill says: Effie Strange — cleverer than the company finds comfortable, spendthrift, adored and exhausting; always short of money. Of Dr Tobias Quill: Dr Tobias Quill — a nervous physician and coroner; supplies the company its remedies.\n\nThe tower proved every pair of hands but one.",
